            <ArticleTitle>Subpleural catheter placement for pain relief after thoracoscopic resection.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1522-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Infusion of local anesthetics into an extrapleural pocket results in excellent postoperative pain relief through a multilevel intercostal nerve blockade. This report describes a simple, rapid technique of subpleural catheter placement that lends itself well to thoracoscopic procedures.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
